<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Midterms 2026: Democrats win control of House and Senate as Republican strongholds fall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c35be0c1ba8af1ab81e0f7e88d32b5fef32f0fb504641ef322ba8f0ada071fec</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T06:27:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>Midterms: Why is California slower at counting its votes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c03f8ccaff331c21f13b4e1ae09cf4be3e75ce5ace5de5169fb3d081d1072121</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:20:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-midterms-why-is-california-slower-at-counting-its-votes" /><summary type="html">California polls have just closed, but results will take longer to come in. Why does the state take longer to count its votes? We discuss this with our guest, Guy Marzorati, political correspondent at KQED in the Bay Area.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: "Keeping our fingers crossed" (Leila Meresman)</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5a8f4dc874e704501c84d06980014efe608e9375239003751964d84e82d8a1c</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:15:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-keeping-our-fingers-crossed-leila-meresman" /><summary type="html">Democrats who once saw the political map as an almost impossible lift are now hopeful that a Senate majority is within reach, even though their path runs through several more conservative states. 

 We discuss this with our guest Leila Meresman, spokesperson of Democrats Abroad France says.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Democrats celebrate early victories at a watch party in Los Angeles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c9a7b7521e4f454e423dac74da4012ba5591836db0933b66b0aa39fafe51150</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:12:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-democrats-celebrate-early-victories-at-a-watch-party-in-los-angeles" /><summary type="html">Our correspondent Wassim Cornet reports from a Democratic watch party in Los Angeles where "people are opening bottles of champagne" following the Democrats' first victories in these midterm elections. We also speak with France 24's Jessica Le Masurier, reporting from Detroit, Michigan.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Midterms live : Democrats take control of Senate, ending Republican dominance in Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05e18c7c2ded6bdb45332d139da293e9902d3b50bb707f0f14192d3395f82d23</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T04:37:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Midterms live: Texas, Ohio, North and South Carolina... Democrats have already flipped 4 Senate seats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64d4c4bca4b6fc11c8d7303e049b38dee38af91c4cee6cebbbcf03fd49e1623a</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T04:18:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>Key US Senate results: Democrats win upper chamber with victories in Texas and Iowa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cd26027c547004236ae288ceac3200ce97a44b2ed5431a483c94e14c1b4197a</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T03:52:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-key-us-senate-results-democrats-wrest-north-and-south-carolina-from-the-republicans" /><summary type="html">Democrats won control of the Senate in the US midterm elections Tuesday, with initial results showing the party securing shock victories in Texas, Ohio, North and South Carolina, Kansas and Iowa.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: "Voters have become increasingly frustrated with President Trump"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e41d930e0efccd7b44514c1292afa429a1e648e9e7864197b86c9639937c9196</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T03:50:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-voters-have-become-increasingly-frustrated-with-president-trump" /><summary type="html">The polls in these midterm elections suggest that "this will either be a good night or a historic night for Democrats". But what is driving this momentum? We discuss this with our guest, Mallory Newall, Senior Vice President at Ipsos.

"We've seen in our polling at Ipsos in recent weeks and months that voters have become increasingly frustrated with President Trump," she says.</summary></entry><entry><title>US: "Even in places where the Democrats haven't won, the swing towards them has been significant"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d0f06a94b6617730899c5a0fa478551a403c3796fa546b3d31902b96aa3539c</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T03:48:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-even-in-places-where-the-democrats-haven-t-won-the-swing-towards-them-has-been-significant" /><summary type="html">Tens of millions of Americans cast their vote in the crucial polls that have been pitched as a referendum on Donald Trump's presidency amid anger at surging petrol prices, tariffs and the Iran war. We discuss the first results with France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani and Fraser Jackson. "Even in places where the Democrats haven't won, the swing towards them has been significant", he says.</summary></entry><entry><title>Democratic gains mount in US midterms as Trump faces bruising verdict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cb4e10823b7adc3c9230a043b3ffa63c3b9b7a72378e080858142c945abb10b</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T03:41:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-democratic-gains-mount-in-us-midterms-as-trump-faces-bruising-verdict" /><summary type="html">Democrats notched a string of early victories in US midterm elections Tuesday, flipping a Republican-held Senate seat and making inroads in conservative House districts as President Donald Trump faced the prospect of a bruising election setback. France 24's Douglas Herbert gives us his analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Georgia Senator Jon Ossoff wins reelection</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6be1756a30fb8a492b7a38bb9001f315b90087f9c2cbe2f22480eaba20f2da6a</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T03:36:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-replay-georgia-senator-jon-ossoff-wins-reelection" /><summary type="html">Georgia Senator Jon Ossoff was reelected Tuesday to a second term, holding a key seat for Democrats by defeating Republican Representative Mike Collins in a race that catapulted the Senate’s youngest member to the forefront of his party’s national stars as it looks to stymie President Donald Trump in his final years in the White House.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms: Abdul El-Sayed, Mike Rogers face off for Michigan Senate seat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f76ebc30735e8db23b43e01819de3061975ddb4acb5b514aa3a8ac6ca4aec513</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T02:53:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-midterms-abdul-el-sayed-mike-rogers-face-off-for-michigan-senate-seat" /><summary type="html">With New Hampshire and Georgia staying in Democratic hands, Republicans now look to Michigan for a pickup, where Democrat Abdul El-Sayed is competing with Republican Mike Rogers. France 24's Jessica Le Masurier reports from a Democratic watch party in Detroit.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Democrats flip Senate seat in North Carolina</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d65ace8aed2b75095b7e6b4586db9e041616f0daecb591c3f33c328dd6078d28</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T02:46:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-democrats-flip-senate-seat-in-north-carolina" /><summary type="html">Democrats have flipped a Senate seat in North Carolina as they try to recapture majorities in Congress and break Republicans’ unified hold on power in Washington. France 24's Florence Villeminot walks us through the US electoral map.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Midterms live: Democrat Roy Cooper flips first Senate seat, follow the results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02ab13300b2d9dc5d143cd97621108ca606119010165ef2b079ba0b451f3ce9f</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T01:38:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>US democracy, Trump fatigue, cost of living are top issues with voters, AP survey finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b82a650322a1b6eade75a55a4fa40239fab80eb0fb7292b5000158c05f9f6671</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T23:46:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-trump-fatigue-cost-of-living-and-corruption-are-top-issues-with-us-voters-ap-survey-finds" /><summary type="html">Roughly 6 in 10 voters deeply disapprove of US President Donald Trump's presidency, according to an AP survey released Tuesday. About 4 in 10 say the economy is the most important issue while 3 in 10 say the state of US democracy is of primary concern – well above the number that rated crime or immigration as most important.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Historian Timothy Snyder: Trump running US foreign policy 'as though he were an organized criminal'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26e7498d5286ee6f10c2d9c5ce45000073a32b0fa5c4761418572ad2746b36d0</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T22:28:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261103-historian-timothy-snyder-trump-running-us-foreign-policy-as-though-he-were-an-organized-criminal" /><summary type="html">As Americans head to the polls for the midterm elections, François Picard welcomes historian Timothy Snyder, professor at the University of Toronto's Munk School of Global Affairs, for a conversation about the future of American democracy, the growing political influence of technology billionaires and the dangers of a new Gilded Age. Who really holds power in Donald Trump's America: the president or the billionaires surrounding him?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump tariffs hitting small businesses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63673c9685735b8d9889e3ec8cfc9b01fa1cba9e0c320ffd61f2a98870aa7245</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T21:45:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261103-trump-tariffs-hitting-small-businesses" /><summary type="html">As US voters cast their ballots in the midterm elections, the economy remained their top concern. Despite robust headline macroeconomic data, middle-class Americans are growing increasingly frustrated with the rising cost of living. Meanwhile, Donald Trump's tariffs have hit small businesses hard, leading to a significant rise in bankruptcies. Our correspondents met with some business owners.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa braces for some job losses as AGOA ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:026705df6c39b9a8ecdf1bbcc4b6220e6d7ee69e81e7e473a769495b2db83875</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T21:18:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-braces-for-some-job-losses-as-agoa-ends" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Rwanda and South Africa will lose their duty-free access to the U.S. market after being excluded from the AGOA trade program. Also, South Africans head to the polls amid water shortages and frustration with local services. And  in the DRC's mining capital, Kolwezi, residents are taking on one of the country's largest Chinese-owned mines... accusing it of poisoning their environment.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Trump promised a 'Golden Age'. What has he delivered at home?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a185518a9fa7a1f5ceb6acd3cba69064da3e7b727c48e29a63033b69e2d96635</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:56:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261103-trump-promised-a-golden-age-what-has-he-delivered-at-home" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump promised Americans a “Golden Age” when he returned to the White House in January 2025. Since then, his administration has slashed government spending through DOGE, ramped up mass deportations, expanded ICE operations and pursued an aggressive crackdown on DEI programmes and transgender rights. But how much has he actually achieved, and at what cost? Vedika Bahl examines Trump's domestic agenda since returning to office.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Trickle or tsunami? Democrats eye gains in US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9d7d4f2bd833e08385026c0c0e8d980de10212c1d546a79c5cd89051dc36228</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T19:18:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261103-trickle-or-tsunami-democrats-eye-gains-in-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Will it be a trickle, a wave, or a tsunami? Election Day in the United States with Democrats hoping to take back one or both houses of Congress. We’ll track the turnout, gauge the mood and raise the curtain ahead of Midterms results that are sure to shape the last two years of Donald Trump’s second and final term. Will a US president who’s already broken norms with his maximum use of executive powers be affected by the results a little, a lot, or not at all?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Midterms live: Voting under way to determine control of Congress and the future of Trump's agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0866900273ca166618aebb9bb6263c5086144fa8c72ebd55ff1dc0aefd60257</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T18:42:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>France's dermatology crisis: Patients desperate for appointments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02751e826d8ebb1596e48c050380482f470e6f1767b4ba51e3893ace35727e7e</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:34:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20261103-france-s-dermatology-crisis-patients-desperate-for-appointments" /><summary type="html">Around 200,000 cases of skin cancer are diagnosed in France every year. Yet as more and more patients seek medical advice, getting an appointment with a dermatologist is becoming increasingly difficult. Half the country's dermatologists are nearing retirement, and only around 100 new specialists are trained up each year. Faced with this growing shortage, some are coming up with innovative solutions. FRANCE 24's Aurore Dupuis and Sonia Baritello report.</summary><category term="France in focus" /></entry><entry><title>Family wealth, Epstein, ‘vanity projects’: How Democrats plan to investigate Trump after midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c631dad35d423c18a8a625eacf207c5c415e12b6a10d53f61f9d6dc8f42c9b84</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:30:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-trump-family-wealth-epstein-vanity-projects-democrats-plan-to-investigate-after-midterms" /><summary type="html">Democrats are preparing to launch a flurry of investigations into President Donald Trump’s administration and business dealings if they retake one or both chambers of Congress, devising strategies to circumvent obstruction from the White House and avoid the impeachment deadlock that consumed the US legislature during Trump’s first term in office.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Russian households face increasing financial strain as war in Ukraine drags on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86c6b123675d6f31003f6c94686e7e3f1345f1c546928b1610d15e524a593b0e</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:05:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-russian-households-face-increasing-financial-strain-as-war-in-ukraine-drags-on" /><summary type="html">As Moscow continues to launch strikes across Ukraine, Russian citizens are facing increasing financial strain. Since the start of the war in 2022, utility bills in Russia have risen by more than 50% – over 13% this year alone. These rising costs come as the country grapples with ongoing drone attacks originating from Ukraine.</summary></entry></feed>
